    return `<article class="upset-research"><div class="eyebrow">UPSET RESEARCH · PROSPECTIVE TEST</div><h2>Does the matchup upgrade help?</h2><p>${n?`${n} completed games with both forecasts saved before kickoff.`:'The experiment has started. No completed games with eligible pregame pairs have been graded yet.'} Both wins and losses count. The experiment does not change the main picks.</p>${n?`<div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Measure</th><th>Main model</th><th>Experimental model</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Winner record</td><td>${score(a.winnerRecord)}</td><td>${score(b.winnerRecord)}</td></tr><tr><td>Average margin error ↓</td><td>${a.marginMAE.toFixed(2)}</td><td>${b.marginMAE.toFixed(2)}</td></tr><tr><td>Probability error (Brier) ↓</td><td>${a.brier.toFixed(3)}</td><td>${b.brier.toFixed(3)}</td></tr><tr><td>Outright underdog picks</td><td>${score(a.upsetRecord)}</td><td>${score(b.upsetRecord)}</td></tr></tbody></table></div>`:''}<p class="tiny">${esc(trial.method)} This comparison covers all eligible games and does not follow the main-record filters above.</p><a href="upset-research-results.json" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">View the experiment record ↗</a></article>`;
  }
